Central tenant of our project is 

	RISK = IMPACT * PROBABILITY

Specific user risk equals total dollar amount that an identity theft event could cost within a year including time lost to recovery times the probability of identity theft occurring given a data breach by a specific company within a year

Impact - Depends on user situation. Based on default values or if survey results

Impact = Credit + Savings + Average Time Spent Dealing with identity theft * Hourly Rate

Credit = Available Credit or Possible Available credit Based on Credit Score Survey Question
Poor Fair  Good Excellent
  $0 $500 $1000     $1500
Default is average U.S. credit limit

Hourly Rate Survey Question to nearest $5 = Salary Survey Question to neared $5000 / 40 hours / week / 52 week / year
Hourly Rate * Average Time Spent Dealing with Identity Theft
Default is average U.S. wage

Saving - Survey Question to nearest $5000
Default is average U.S. savings


Probability - Depends on what the user shared with the service and service breach history
Probability = Average Chance of Identity theft given breach * Chance of breach * Chance of any user being involved * Average chance of any covered data being involved * Chance data would be used in an identity theft event

times % Chance that Identity theft occurs given a data breach occurred
	From Identity theft report

times % Chance a company will have a data breach based on historical data
	current year - year of first breach / total breaches = % chance of breach per year

times % Average Chance of any user being involved per breach 
